-In Desktop **Settings → General → Update channel**, **Stable** selects `stable` and **Development** selects `nightly`. Publishers choose versions for each channel independently of version suffixes; Stable can also deliver alpha or RC versions. The main process saves `updates.channel` in this same file and applies the choice immediately through IPC; no Host settings service is involved. An omitted channel uses the build-injected package default. External edits and deletion are read only on the next launch; no file watcher runs. The authentication-popup setting remains startup-only. UI writes retain unrelated fields from the latest valid document; external editors must not write concurrently with a UI save.
-
